            "text": "Particles from cooking, such as smoke from searing, clear in roughly the same 30 to 60 minutes as other fine particles. The smell itself is gas and depends on the carbon filter, so it clears more slowly, often over an hour or two with a good carbon stage. A range hood vented outside removes cooking smells far faster than any purifier."
          }
        }
      ],
