        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The honest answer to how long an air purifier takes is that it depends on two numbers you can look up: your room's volume and the purifier's smoke CADR. Divide one by the other, multiply by three, and you have a realistic time to a noticeably cleaner room with the door closed and the fan on high. For a well-sized unit that is usually 30 to 60 minutes.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If the math says hours, the purifier is too small for the room, the setting is too low, or the door is open. Fix those, then leave it running on auto so the room stays clean instead of just getting clean once.
          </p>
